h of $22.28. Volume that day was 3.7M shares, 2.19x the prior 10-day average of 1.7M. It didn't hold. By Jan 30, 2017 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $19.00.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}